        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Netanyahu directs Israeli forces to expand Gaza control to 70 percent Issued on: 29/05/2026 - 12:02 Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said on Thursday he had directed Israel's military to take more of Gaza, initially by seizing 70% of the Palestinian territory, where the population is already penned into a tiny strip of land along the coast. Israel effectively controls an estimated 64% of the tiny coastal ​Strip, bombarded to ‌ruins by Israel's two-year military assault that followed the 2023 Hamas attack on southern Israel. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Kethevane Gorjestani tells us more. Possible Iran-US deal: Tehran denies final text has been agreed 29/05/2026 Israel carries out strike on Beirut suburbs, first near capital in weeks 28/05/2026 Brazil's Lula backs new oil, gas drilling in western Amazon 28/05/2026 Gaza children with Down syndrome are still reckoning with the devastation of the war 28/05/2026 Iran: US base targeted in missile strike 28/05/2026 France: 'We must consider the effect climate policies will have on the poorest' 28/05/2026 Israel strikes Beirut southern suburb ahead of crucial Washington talks 28/05/2026 Ukraine asks Trump for more US air defence help against Russian missile attacks 28/05/2026 Iran condemns US ceasefire 'violations' after strikes in south 28/05/2026"
