        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Possible Iran-US deal: Tehran denies final text has been agreed On the ground Issued on: 29/05/2026 - 12:00 Modified: 29/05/2026 - 12:01 The United States and Iran appear to have the draft text of an agreement to extend their ceasefire for 60 days and provide a framework to negotiate longer-term peace. But there have been conflicting reports from sources in Washington and Tehran about what might be covered in the initial agreement – and what is off the table. FRANCE 24’s correspondent Reza Sayah tells us more about what Iranian officials have been saying. Netanyahu directs Israeli forces to expand Gaza control to 70 percent 29/05/2026 Israel carries out strike on Beirut suburbs, first near capital in weeks 28/05/2026 Brazil's Lula backs new oil, gas drilling in western Amazon 28/05/2026 Gaza children with Down syndrome are still reckoning with the devastation of the war 28/05/2026 Iran: US base targeted in missile strike 28/05/2026 France: 'We must consider the effect climate policies will have on the poorest' 28/05/2026 Israel strikes Beirut southern suburb ahead of crucial Washington talks 28/05/2026 Ukraine asks Trump for more US air defence help against Russian missile attacks 28/05/2026 Iran condemns US ceasefire 'violations' after strikes in south 28/05/2026"
